meta {
  name: 3.Get Report Status
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/reports/{{reportid}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Step 3 of the Reports flow — the "Get Report Details" endpoint. Take the report ID from the
  response in "2.Create Report" and populate the collection variable `{{reportid}}` with the
  reference. Use this endpoint to check whether the report is ready to download.

  **Parameters**
  - `reportId` (path) — bound to `{{reportid}}`.

  **Usage**: Poll this until `status` shows as complete, then take the `downloadURL` field from the
  response and use it in "4.Get Report" to actually retrieve the file.

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/reports/get-report-details

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}

